Generic single-database configuration.

To generate a new revision file, run:

```
python -m tiled.authn_database revision -m "description..."
```

Besides the usual alembic identifiers, a migration script may declare:

```
required_at_startup = False
```

At startup, the server checks the revision of the database. By default
(`required_at_startup = True`, or no declaration), the server refuses to
start unless this migration has been applied.

With `required_at_startup = False`, the server may start on a database that
is at the previous revision, and logs a warning. Use this when the server does
not need the migration in order to work, for example when the migration only
adds an index or fixes a constraint. Then the new version of Tiled can be
deployed first and the database upgraded afterwards.

This applies to the latest database revision only. A database that is two or more
migrations behind is always refused, whatever the migrations declare.
